INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'ai-training-jobs-consultants-20261104', 'global', 'USA',
'AI Training Jobs for Consultants: 148 Roles Paying $55 to $145 an Hour',
'',
'As of 4 November 2026, 148 AI training jobs for consultants and business experts are open across 20 platforms, with typical pay of $55 to $145 an hour and a median of $70 an hour.',
'',
$$<p>As of 4 November 2026, AI training jobs for consultants number 148 open roles across 20 AI training platforms, with typical pay running from $55 to $145 an hour and a median of $70 an hour, according to a live count checked against each platform's job board every hour. AI training jobs for consultants are hourly contract roles in which experienced business professionals grade a model's business reasoning, build the analyses and plans it is tested on, and write what an experienced professional would write. The highest advertised rate in the count is $400 an hour, at Surge AI, but most roles sit far below that ceiling, and 20 of the 148 roles state no hourly rate at all, so the headline figures describe only the roles that publish pay.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Count date</th><td>4 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Open roles for consultants and business experts</th><td>148, across 20 AI training platforms</td></tr>
<tr><th>Typical hourly pay</th><td>$55 to $145 an hour, median $70</td></tr>
<tr><th>Highest advertised rate</th><td>$400 an hour, at Surge AI</td></tr>
<tr><th>Roles stating pay</th><td>128 of 148; 20 state no hourly rate</td></tr>
<tr><th>Rates measured</th><td>94 distinct advertised rates, across 13 platforms</td></tr>
<tr><th>Work type</th><td>Remote, hourly contract work; hours depend on the project</td></tr>
<tr><th>Usual first step</th><td>A role assessment or an AI interview, then an identity check</td></tr>
<tr><th>Application fee</th><td>None; a legitimate platform never charges you to apply</td></tr>
</table>
<h2>AI training jobs for consultants: what the work actually involves</h2>
<p>The work splits by specialty, and the count groups the 148 roles accordingly. Management consultants, strategists and business leaders account for 49 roles: building and grading the analyses, decisions and decks a model produces. Marketing, brand and sales account for 42 roles: judging a model's campaigns, copy, pitches and plans the way a senior marketer or seller would. Operations, supply chain, project and product management account for 36 roles: grading a model's answers where practice matters, from logistics and procurement to programme management. Risk, compliance and fraud account for 11 roles: checking a model's answers on controls, regulation and investigations the way a practitioner would. HR and recruiting account for 10 roles: grading a model's answers on hiring, policy and employee relations, in English and other languages.</p>
<p>None of this is client work. The platforms pay consultants, marketers, salespeople, HR, operations, supply chain and project professionals by the hour to train and evaluate AI models, not to advise a company. That distinction matters for anyone already employed: the platforms themselves warn applicants to check their contract's outside-work and confidentiality clauses first, and never to bring client or employer documents into a task.</p>
<h2>AI training jobs for consultants: pay by specialty</h2>
<p>Pay varies sharply by specialty, and the site measures each specialty's typical pay over its own open roles only where at least three distinct rates are posted. Management consultants, strategists and business leaders typically earn $55 to $150 an hour, with the highest rate at $400 an hour. Marketing, brand and sales typically earn $50 to $150 an hour, with the highest rate at $350 an hour. Operations, supply chain, project and product management typically earn $60 to $125 an hour, with the highest rate at $150 an hour. Risk, compliance and fraud typically earn $70 to $125 an hour, with the highest rate at $125 an hour. HR and recruiting typically earn $35 to $70 an hour, with the highest rate at $90 an hour.</p>
<p>Those bands come with two warnings worth reading before applying. First, 34 of the roles advertise only a maximum rate, such as "up to $X an hour", and those maximum-only figures are excluded from the typical-pay bands. Second, hourly pay is not a salary: hours depend on the project, so ask how hours are assigned before treating a headline rate as income.</p>
<h2>Who is hiring consultants for AI training work</h2>
<p>Twenty platforms hold the 148 roles, and a handful hold most of them. SuperAnnotate (SME) lists 19 roles, micro1 lists 17, AfterQuery lists 17, Mercor lists 15, Handshake AI lists 13, Aligned Labs lists 11 and Invisible lists 11. Surge AI lists only 5 roles but carries the highest advertised rate, at $55 to $400 an hour, while Mercor's range runs $36 to $350 an hour and Aligned Labs runs $40 to $150 an hour. The spread shows why platform choice matters: the same background can be worth very different rates depending on where it is listed.</p>
<p>What the roles ask for is read from the requirements of 143 of the 148 open roles. Of those, 48 ask for a bachelor's degree or a degree, 85 name years of experience, 6 ask where the applicant lives or may work, 3 ask for a professional licence and 1 asks for a certification. Only 1 asks for coding, such as Python or SQL, which separates this market clearly from the coding side of AI training work covered in <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ai-training-jobs-software-engineers-20261104">AI training jobs for software engineers</a>. The roles that name experience ask for a median of 5 years, so this is work for people who can already do the job in real life, not an entry route into consulting.</p>
<h2>How to apply for AI training jobs for consultants</h2>
<p>Start with the live board: the count at <a href="https://aitraining.jobs/ai-training-jobs-for-consultants?country=all">AITraining.jobs</a> links each role to the platform that posted it, and each platform runs its own process. The usual pattern is a profile setting out experience and credentials, a role assessment or a recorded AI interview, and then an identity check before any paid work begins. Mercor, for example, runs an on-camera AI interview with role-specific questions and a background check that typically takes one to two weeks, with government ID and a selfie video verified through Persona. DataAnnotation, micro1, AfterQuery and Turing run similar checks, each with its own version of a government photo ID plus a selfie, and some platforms repeat the check for each new offer.</p>
<p>Prepare for the assessment the way the work itself is judged: with a short, specific example of professional judgement, not a general claim of expertise. Keep client material out of every answer, and keep a record of which platform each application went to, since several platforms recruit for the same underlying AI labs. Finally, never pay to apply: the platforms in this count state plainly that a legitimate platform never charges applicants, and any message asking for a fee, a deposit or a training payment is a sign to stop. The wider AI hiring picture, including <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ai-startup-jobs-13514-roles-20261104">13,514 roles open at 1,100 AI startups</a>, shows the same rule holding across the market: real employers pay you, not the other way round.</p>
<p><small>Sources: AITraining.jobs, "AI Training Jobs for Consultants", figures as of 4 November 2026, checked against each platform's job board; field-level research "Expert Fields in Demand for AI Training", data from 7 October 2026 to 3 November 2026.</small></p>$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://aitraining.jobs/ai-training-jobs-for-consultants?country=all'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'robot-training-jobs-1136-roles-20261104', 'global', 'USA',
'Robot Training Jobs: 1,136 Roles Open as Fleet Work Falls and Tesla Hires',
'',
'Robot training jobs number 1,136 open roles on the RobotTraining.jobs board at the end of 3 November 2026, with fleet operations falling and Tesla posting the most new roles in the week.',
'',
$$<p>Robot training jobs number 1,136 open roles on the RobotTraining.jobs board at the end of 3 November 2026, up from 1,126 at the start of the week of 28 October to 3 November 2026, according to the board's weekly report published on 4 November 2026. Robot training jobs are the hands-on roles behind self-driving cars, delivery robots and warehouse machines: driving, supervising and demonstrating for robots, operating them remotely, and recording the human movements and decisions their models learn from. The headline rise needs one qualification before it is read as hiring growth: the board started reading 21 more employers during the week, led by HireArt with 26 roles, and among the 86 employers it read all week, openings actually fell 5.9 per cent, to 1,066, with 41 new listings against 108 removed.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Report week</th><td>28 October to 3 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Open roles on the board</th><td>1,136 at the end of 3 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Comparable employers</th><td>86 employers read all week; openings fell 5.9% to 1,066</td></tr>
<tr><th>New listings in the week</th><td>41, against 108 removed</td></tr>
<tr><th>Largest kind of work</th><td>Autonomous vehicle and drone operators: 540 roles on the board</td></tr>
<tr><th>Robot fleet operations</th><td>226 roles on the board; 257 to 207 on comparable employers</td></tr>
<tr><th>Biggest employer</th><td>Tesla: 172 roles, after 22 new listings in the week</td></tr>
<tr><th>Median posted pay</th><td>$30.50 an hour for autonomous vehicle and drone operators; $27 for fleet operations</td></tr>
<tr><th>Application fee</th><td>None on the employers' own careers pages; never pay to apply</td></tr>
</table>
<h2>Robot training jobs: what moved in the week</h2>
<p>Fleet work fell the most. Robot fleet operations dropped from 257 to 207 roles on comparable employers, as 62 listings came down and 12 went up, while its median posted pay held at $27 an hour. Avride accounted for much of the fall, going from 45 open roles to 12, and Amazon Prime Air went from 70 to 55 in the week it began drone deliveries in Nampa, Idaho, to homes within 7.5 miles of its fulfilment centre. Autonomous vehicle and drone operator roles eased from 520 to 511, with 26 listings removed and 17 new, at a median of $30.32 an hour on the comparable set. Tesla moved the other way, posting the most new roles in the week at 22, and reaching 172 open roles in total.</p>
<p>Smaller categories moved in both directions. Egocentric and wearable capture slipped from 139 to 132 roles, as RemoExperts took down all 6 of its head-camera postings and micro1 went from 8 to 5, and the median posted capture pay fell from $15 to $13 an hour. Demonstration collection held at 123 roles with a median of $30.50 an hour, teleoperation stood at 71 roles with a median of $28 an hour, and robot evaluation rose from 8 to 10 roles, among them a remote Sovrano AI robotics expert role at $40 to $125 an hour.</p>
<h2>Where the money for robot data is going</h2>
<p>The funding news explains who buys the demonstrations, teleoperation hours and annotated video these roles produce. GenRobot AI, a Beijing company that builds the equipment and software for turning recordings of people's work into robot training data, disclosed a $100 million Series A+ round from investors including SAIC Motor, Baidu and Galaxy General Robotics. WeRide's data and world-model unit Jingshuo agreed to raise 70 million yuan, about $9.9 million, and CNTXT AI said it will open 30,000 square feet of robotics-data facilities in Dubai and Abu Dhabi, where workers wear motion-sensor suits or light head-mounted cameras to record home and workplace tasks, the first of them from November.</p>
<p>On the fleet side, shareholders of Churchill Capital Corp XI approved its merger with Agility Robotics, the maker of the Digit humanoid, which is expected to raise about $465 million and list Agility on Nasdaq. Waymo chose Toyota's 2027 bZ4X as its robotaxi for right-hand-drive markets, with Toyota building it with Waymo's system at its Takaoka plant, testing starting in Japan, and the United Kingdom named as the next market. Aurora said it has more than 20 driverless trucks built and expects to build 20 a week from early December, toward annual capacity of more than 1,000, though supplier problems pushed its goal of 200 trucks on the road to February.</p>
<h2>Robot training jobs: what the work asks of you</h2>
<p>Most robot training jobs are physical and tied to a place, which is the single most important limit in this market. Fleet operators, safety drivers and vehicle operators work where the vehicles run, drone operators work within a delivery zone, and capture workers wear suits or cameras in a facility or a home. The board's new employers show the shape of that demand: HireArt recruits robot operators, safety drivers and vehicle operators for robotics and self-driving clients, and the other new boards include Kiwibot, Latitude AI, Arctic Engines, Coco Robotics, Starship, Matternet and PlusAI. A driving licence, a clean record and willingness to work shifts are the usual entry conditions for operator roles.</p>
<p>The exception is the smaller set of remote roles, and they pay more because they need more judgement. The remote Sovrano AI robotics expert role at $40 to $125 an hour is an evaluation role, judging a robot's work rather than driving it, and it sits in the same higher-paid band as demonstration collection at a $30.50 median. That split mirrors the wider AI training market, where <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ai-training-jobs-software-engineers-20261104">AI training jobs for software engineers</a> pay more for review and evaluation than for routine labelling, and where <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ai-contact-centre-jobs-south-korea-redesign-20261103">AI contact-centre roles in South Korea</a> are being redesigned around the same judgement work. Applicants from Nepal should weigh the location limit honestly: most robot training roles require presence where a fleet operates, so the realistic route in is a remote evaluation or annotation role, or a role with an employer operating in a country where the applicant can legally work.</p>
<h2>How to apply for robot training jobs</h2>
<p>Start with the weekly report itself at <a href="https://robottraining.jobs/news/2026-11-04">RobotTraining.jobs</a>, where every count opens the live list behind it, then follow the link to the employer's own careers page for the role that fits. Check three things before applying: the location and whether the role is genuinely on site, the licence or driving requirement for operator roles, and the posted pay band against the medians in the report. Because the board's list keeps changing after the week ends, treat the 1,136 figure as a snapshot at the end of 3 November 2026, not a standing total, and re-check the live list on the day of applying. Never pay anyone who promises to place you in such a role.</p>
<p><small>Sources: RobotTraining.jobs, "Robot Training Jobs This Week: Fleet Openings Fall, GenRobot Raises $100M, Aurora Speeds Up Truck Builds", published 4 November 2026, covering 28 October to 3 November 2026; funding items as reported by TechNode, The AI Insider, The National, SEC filing, TechCrunch, Aurora Innovation and DroneXL, as cited in the report.</small></p>$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://robottraining.jobs/news/2026-11-04'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'indian-bank-apprentice-1500-posts-20261104', 'global', 'India',
'Indian Bank Apprentice Recruitment 2026: 1,500 Posts, Applications Open 5 November',
'',
'Indian Bank apprentice recruitment 2026 offers 1,500 apprenticeship training seats, with online applications open from 5 November 2026 to 25 November 2026 and a monthly stipend of Rs. 12,300 to Rs. 15,000.',
'',
$$<p>Indian Bank apprentice recruitment 2026 offers 1,500 apprenticeship training seats for the financial year 2026-27, under an updated notification dated 4 November 2026, with applications open from 5 November 2026 to 25 November 2026. State plainly first: this is a 12-month apprenticeship, not a regular bank job, with a monthly stipend, on-the-job training in a branch, and no guarantee of permanent employment afterwards. Candidates who completed graduation in any discipline between 1 April 2022 and 1 November 2026 can apply, the age limit is 20 to 28 years as on 1 November 2026, with applicable relaxation, and applications go through the NATS 2.0 portal.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Training seats</th><td>1,500, across 30 States and Union Territories</td></tr>
<tr><th>Updated notification date</th><td>4 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Applications open</th><td>5 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Applications close</th><td>25 November 2026, including fee payment and form edits</td></tr>
<tr><th>Monthly stipend</th><td>Rs. 15,000 in metro/urban branches; Rs. 12,300 in rural/semi-urban branches</td></tr>
<tr><th>Training duration</th><td>12 months, on the job, under the Apprentices Act, 1961</td></tr>
<tr><th>Qualification</th><td>Graduation in any discipline, completed between 1 April 2022 and 1 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Age limit</th><td>20 to 28 years as on 1 November 2026, with applicable relaxation</td></tr>
<tr><th>Application fee</th><td>Rs. 800 plus GST (General, OBC, EWS); Rs. 175 plus GST (SC, ST, PwBD)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Selection</th><td>Online test, Local Language Proficiency Test and verification; exam date not announced</td></tr>
</table>
<h2>Indian Bank apprentice recruitment 2026: who can apply</h2>
<p>The qualification rule is narrow and catches out more applicants than any other condition. Candidates must hold a graduate degree in any discipline from a recognised university or a Central Government-recognised equivalent, completed between 1 April 2022 and 1 November 2026, with the final result declared on or before 1 November 2026. Candidates who passed graduation before 1 April 2022 are not eligible, and candidates awaiting a final result after 1 November 2026 are not eligible either. Final-year students whose results are still pending therefore cannot apply under this notification.</p>
<p>Two further exclusions apply. Candidates who have already undergone apprenticeship training, are currently undergoing it, or had an apprenticeship terminated due to their own fault cannot apply, and candidates with one year or more of work experience after completing their qualification are also ineligible. The age limit is 20 to 28 years as on 1 November 2026, which the notification expresses for General and EWS candidates as a date-of-birth range from 2 November 1998 to 1 November 2006, both dates inclusive. Relaxation applies as prescribed: 5 years for SC and ST candidates, 3 years for OBC non-creamy layer candidates, 10 years for persons with benchmark disabilities, and the prescribed limits for eligible widows, divorced and legally separated women who have not remarried. Check the full conditions in the 44-page updated advertisement before paying the fee.</p>
<h2>Stipend, seats and where the posts are</h2>
<p>The stipend depends on where the branch sits. Apprentices in metro and urban branches receive Rs. 15,000 a month, made up of up to Rs. 8,850 from the bank and up to Rs. 6,150 from the government, while apprentices in rural and semi-urban branches receive Rs. 12,300 a month, made up of up to Rs. 6,150 from each side. The stipend is not a regular bank employee salary, and apprentices are not eligible for additional allowances or regular employee benefits. Apprentices earn one casual leave on completion of each month, with a maximum of four at a time, overtime is not permitted, and more than 338 paid days during the 12 months are required to become eligible for the Certificate of Proficiency, issued digitally through NATS 2.0 after successful training and assessment.</p>
<p>The 1,500 seats are spread across 30 States and Union Territories, and the distribution matters when choosing a preferred location. Uttar Pradesh has the highest number at 285, followed by Tamil Nadu at 270 and West Bengal at 145, while smaller States and Union Territories hold only one or two seats each. By category, the seats break down as 676 Unreserved, 348 Other Backward Classes, 252 Scheduled Caste, 142 Economically Weaker Section and 82 Scheduled Tribe, with 48 PwBD seats reserved horizontally within the total, not in addition to it. The advertised seats are tentative and may change according to the bank's actual requirements, and Annexure III of the notification gives the district-wise distribution, which candidates should check before choosing preferred districts. The apprentice route is distinct from other large openings covered on this site, including <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/pgcil-engineer-trainee-319-posts-20261103">319 engineer trainee posts at Power Grid</a> and <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/dsssb-delhi-court-641-posts-20261104">641 Delhi court posts under DSSSB</a>: it is training with a stipend, not a permanent post.</p>
<h2>Selection and the online examination</h2>
<p>Selection runs through an online objective examination and a Local Language Proficiency Test, with document verification and medical fitness before engagement, and the bank may also conduct an interview at its discretion. The online examination carries 100 multiple-choice questions for 100 marks in a composite duration of 60 minutes: Reasoning Aptitude 15, Computer Knowledge 10, English Language 25, Quantitative Aptitude 25, and General Awareness with special reference to the banking industry 25. The examination date, the local language test date and the document verification date have not been announced in the advertisement, the bank said, so applicants should watch the official bank website for those dates rather than trusting dates circulated on social media.</p>
<h2>How to apply for Indian Bank apprentice recruitment 2026</h2>
<p>Apply only through the official route, in this order. First, register and complete a profile on the NATS 2.0 apprenticeship portal at <a href="https://nats.education.gov.in">nats.education.gov.in</a>, since the bank's application sits on top of that registration. Second, submit the apprenticeship application for Indian Bank through the bank's portal at <a href="https://indianbank.bank.in">indianbank.bank.in</a> between 5 November 2026 and 25 November 2026, choosing the State or Union Territory and district preferences from the notification's annexures. Third, pay the fee online by debit card, credit card or internet banking within the same window: Rs. 800 plus GST for General, OBC and EWS candidates, and Rs. 175 plus GST for SC, ST and PwBD candidates, non-refundable, with bank transaction charges additional. Edits to the form must also be completed by 25 November 2026.</p>
<p>One caution applies to every applicant. The fee is paid only through the official payment gateway inside the application, and no agent or social media account can secure a seat or guarantee selection. Anyone asking for payment outside the portal, or promising a permanent job after the apprenticeship, is not acting for the bank: the notification states plainly that Indian Bank has no obligation to provide regular or contractual employment after completion of training, and apprentices do not have a right to claim employment with the bank. Read the full 44-page updated advertisement dated 4 November 2026 before applying, and keep the fee receipt safe until verification is complete.</p>
<p><small>Sources: FreeJobAlert summary of the Indian Bank updated notification dated 4 November 2026 for the engagement of 1,500 apprentices for FY 2026-27; Indian Bank official website, indianbank.bank.in; NATS 2.0 apprenticeship portal, nats.education.gov.in.</small></p>$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://www.freejobalert.com/articles/indian-bank-apprentices-recruitment-2026-3078364'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;
